{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form supports synchronous, asynchronous, field-level, form-level, and\nStandard Schema validation. Every validator is an ordered object with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":"\nimplementation and explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"choose-when-validation-runs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose when validation runs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"change"},{"type":"text","value":" for immediate feedback and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blur"},{"type":"text","value":" for feedback after leaving an\ninput. Submission runs validators by default regardless of their configured\nchange and blur triggers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"ageValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'] as const,\n    run: ({ value }: { value: number }) =>\n      value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n  },\n  {\n    triggers: ['blur'] as const,\n    run: ({ value }: { value: number }) =>\n      value >= 0 ? undefined : 'Age cannot be negative',\n  },\n]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<ng-container\n  [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n  name=\"age\"\n  [validators]=\"ageValidators\"\n  #field=\"field\"\n>\n  <label>\n    Age\n    <input\n      type=\"number\"\n      [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n      [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n      (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n      (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.valueAsNumber)\"\n      [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n    />\n    @for (error of field.api.errors; track error) {\n    <span role=\"alert\">{{ error.message }}</span>\n    }\n  </label>\n</ng-container>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Additional controls include:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnMount"},{"type":"text","value":": run once when the form is constructed or when a field or form\ngroup first mounts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":": disable or conditionally enable submit-time execution."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggerDebounceMs"},{"type":"text","value":": debounce change and blur execution."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bailIfInvalid"},{"type":"text","value":": skip this and subsequent validators when an earlier one\nfailed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"trigger objects with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":": enable a trigger conditionally."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"},{"type":"text","value":": rerun a field validator when related fields trigger it."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"control-when-errors-are-visible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Control when errors are visible"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation and presentation are separate. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" decides when\nfield issues appear in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.api.errors"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { injectForm } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  errorVisibility: ({ fieldState, state }) =>\n    fieldState.meta.isBlurred || state.submissionAttempts > 0,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.api.meta.original.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" for the unfiltered issues when debugging\nor building a custom visibility system."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-level-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form-level validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A form validator can produce a form issue and route issues to typed field paths\nwith "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createErrorMap"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { injectForm, injectSelector } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    email: '',\n    phone: '',\n  },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n        const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n        if (!value.email && !value.phone) {\n          errors.form = 'Provide an email address or phone number'\n          errors.fields.email = 'Email is required when phone is empty'\n          errors.fields.phone = 'Phone is required when email is empty'\n        }\n\n        return errors\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nformErrors = injectSelector(this.form, (state) => state.errors)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes form-level issues as an Angular signal. Lower-level\nintegrations can subscribe to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.atom"},{"type":"text","value":" directly. Field-routed issues appear\nin the corresponding "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.api.errors"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"asynchronous-validation-and-debouncing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Asynchronous validation and debouncing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" may return a promise. Put cheap synchronous checks first and use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bailIfInvalid"},{"type":"text","value":" to avoid unnecessary requests:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"usernameValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'] as const,\n    run: ({ value }: { value: string }) =>\n      value.length >= 3 ? undefined : 'Use at least 3 characters',\n  },\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'] as const,\n    triggerDebounceMs: 500,\n    bailIfInvalid: true,\n    run: async ({ value }: { value: string }) => {\n      const available = await checkUsername(value)\n      return available ? undefined : 'That username is already taken'\n    },\n  },\n]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass this array to the field with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[validators]=\"usernameValidators\""},{"type":"text","value":".\nSubmit validation always runs immediately, even when a trigger is debounced.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.api.meta.isValidating"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.state.isValidating"},{"type":"text","value":" expose pending\nwork."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"standard-schema-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard Schema validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Any Standard Schema implementation can be supplied as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { injectForm } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst accountSchema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  age: z.number().min(13),\n})\n\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: { email: '', age: 0 },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: accountSchema,\n    },\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema paths are routed to matching fields. Parsed outputs are available by\nvalidator index in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaOutputs"},{"type":"text","value":" during submit, for example\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaOutputs[0]"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" remains the form's raw editable state rather than\nthe parsed output."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For custom schema routing, call a schema's safe parse API inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" and pass\nits issues to the provided "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseIssues"},{"type":"text","value":" helper."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validate-related-fields","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate related fields"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"},{"type":"text","value":" when one field's validity depends on another:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { FieldValidators } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\ntype DateFormValues = { startDate: string; endDate: string }\n\nendDateValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n    watchFields: ['startDate'],\n    run: ({ value, formApi }) =>\n      value >= formApi.getFieldValue('startDate')\n        ? undefined\n        : 'End date must be on or after the start date',\n  },\n] satisfies FieldValidators<DateFormValues, 'endDate', string>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<ng-container\n  [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n  name=\"endDate\"\n  [validators]=\"endDateValidators\"\n  #field=\"field\"\n>\n  <input\n    type=\"date\"\n    [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n    [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n    (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n    [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n  />\n</ng-container>","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validate-a-scoped-form-group","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate a scoped form group"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackFormGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" creates a v2 group for one concrete section of a form. The\ndirective exports its API as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formGroup"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fieldName"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves a\ngroup-relative name to the concrete form path:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TanStackField, TanStackFormGroup } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport type { FormGroupValidators } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nprofileValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: [],\n    run: ({ value }: { value: { name: string } }) =>\n      value.name.length >= 2 ? undefined : 'Enter a name',\n  },\n] satisfies FormGroupValidators<{ name: string }>\n\nsubmitGroup(event: SubmitEvent, group: { handleSubmit: () => unknown }) {\n  event.preventDefault()\n  void group.handleSubmit()\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<ng-container\n  [tanstackFormGroup]=\"form\"\n  name=\"profile\"\n  [validators]=\"profileValidators\"\n  #profile=\"formGroup\"\n>\n  <form (submit)=\"submitGroup($event, profile.api)\">\n    <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"profile.api\" name=\"name\" #name=\"field\">\n      <input\n        [name]=\"name.api.name\"\n        [value]=\"name.api.value\"\n        (input)=\"name.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n      />\n    </ng-container>\n\n    @for (error of profile.api.state.errors; track error) {\n    <span role=\"alert\">{{ error.message }}</span>\n    }\n    <button type=\"submit\">Continue</button>\n  </form>\n</ng-container>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import both directives in the standalone component. Use a Form Group for a\nscoped section of one form; use reusable field mappings when a component must\nwork with different concrete field paths."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"return-errors-from-submission","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return errors from submission"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Endpoint validation belongs in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":". Return\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createValidationError(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" to feed server issues back into normal form state:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"form = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value, createValidationError }) => {\n    const result = await saveProfile(value)\n\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      return createValidationError({\n        form: 'Could not save the profile',\n        fields: { email: 'This email is already registered' },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return null\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prevent-invalid-submission","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prevent invalid submission"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" skips "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" when validation fails and resolves with\nthe validation errors. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmitInvalid"},{"type":"text","value":" is currently available on form\ngroups; root-form support is planned but not yet implemented. Select\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSubmitting"},{"type":"text","value":" as Angular signals to reflect that state in the\nsubmit UI:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"canSubmit = injectSelector(this.form, (state) => state.canSubmit)\nisSubmitting = injectSelector(this.form, (state) => state.isSubmitting)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<button type=\"submit\" [disabled]=\"!canSubmit() || isSubmitting()\">\n  {{ isSubmitting() ? 'Submitting…' : 'Submit' }}\n</button>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a disabled submit button would hide useful validation feedback, keep it\nfocusable with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-disabled"},{"type":"text","value":" and let "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" report the issues."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"choose-when-validation-runs","text":"Choose when validation runs","level":2},{"id":"control-when-errors-are-visible","text":"Control when errors are visible","level":2},{"id":"form-level-validation","text":"Form-level validation","level":2},{"id":"asynchronous-validation-and-debouncing","text":"Asynchronous validation and debouncing","level":2},{"id":"standard-schema-validation","text":"Standard Schema validation","level":2},{"id":"validate-related-fields","text":"Validate related fields","level":2},{"id":"validate-a-scoped-form-group","text":"Validate a scoped form group","level":2},{"id":"return-errors-from-submission","text":"Return errors from submission","level":2},{"id":"prevent-invalid-submission","text":"Prevent invalid submission","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form supports synchronous, asynchronous, field-level, form-level, and\nStandard Schema validation. Every validator is an ordered object with a `run`\nimplementation and explicit `triggers`.\n\n## Choose when validation runs\n\nUse `change` for immediate feedback and `blur` for feedback after leaving an\ninput. Submission runs validators by default regardless of their configured\nchange and blur triggers.\n\n```ts\nageValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'] as const,\n    run: ({ value }: { value: number }) =>\n      value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n  },\n  {\n    triggers: ['blur'] as const,\n    run: ({ value }: { value: number }) =>\n      value >= 0 ? undefined : 'Age cannot be negative',\n  },\n]\n```\n\n```html\n<ng-container\n  [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n  name=\"age\"\n  [validators]=\"ageValidators\"\n  #field=\"field\"\n>\n  <label>\n    Age\n    <input\n      type=\"number\"\n      [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n      [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n      (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n      (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.valueAsNumber)\"\n      [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n    />\n    @for (error of field.api.errors; track error) {\n    <span role=\"alert\">{{ error.message }}</span>\n    }\n  </label>\n</ng-container>\n```\n\nAdditional controls include:\n\n- `runOnMount`: run once when the form is constructed or when a field or form\n  group first mounts.\n- `runOnSubmit`: disable or conditionally enable submit-time execution.\n- `triggerDebounceMs`: debounce change and blur execution.\n- `bailIfInvalid`: skip this and subsequent validators when an earlier one\n  failed.\n- trigger objects with `when`: enable a trigger conditionally.\n- `watchFields`: rerun a field validator when related fields trigger it.\n\n## Control when errors are visible\n\nValidation and presentation are separate. `errorVisibility` decides when\nfield issues appear in `field.api.errors`:\n\n```ts\nimport { injectForm } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  errorVisibility: ({ fieldState, state }) =>\n    fieldState.meta.isBlurred || state.submissionAttempts > 0,\n})\n```\n\nUse `field.api.meta.original.errors` for the unfiltered issues when debugging\nor building a custom visibility system.\n\n## Form-level validation\n\nA form validator can produce a form issue and route issues to typed field paths\nwith `createErrorMap`:\n\n```ts\nimport { injectForm, injectSelector } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    email: '',\n    phone: '',\n  },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n        const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n        if (!value.email && !value.phone) {\n          errors.form = 'Provide an email address or phone number'\n          errors.fields.email = 'Email is required when phone is empty'\n          errors.fields.phone = 'Phone is required when email is empty'\n        }\n\n        return errors\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nformErrors = injectSelector(this.form, (state) => state.errors)\n```\n\n`injectSelector` exposes form-level issues as an Angular signal. Lower-level\nintegrations can subscribe to `form.atom` directly. Field-routed issues appear\nin the corresponding `field.api.errors`.\n\n## Asynchronous validation and debouncing\n\n`run` may return a promise. Put cheap synchronous checks first and use\n`bailIfInvalid` to avoid unnecessary requests:\n\n```ts\nusernameValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'] as const,\n    run: ({ value }: { value: string }) =>\n      value.length >= 3 ? undefined : 'Use at least 3 characters',\n  },\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'] as const,\n    triggerDebounceMs: 500,\n    bailIfInvalid: true,\n    run: async ({ value }: { value: string }) => {\n      const available = await checkUsername(value)\n      return available ? undefined : 'That username is already taken'\n    },\n  },\n]\n```\n\nPass this array to the field with `[validators]=\"usernameValidators\"`.\nSubmit validation always runs immediately, even when a trigger is debounced.\n`field.api.meta.isValidating` and `form.state.isValidating` expose pending\nwork.\n\n## Standard Schema validation\n\nAny Standard Schema implementation can be supplied as `run`:\n\n```ts\nimport { injectForm } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst accountSchema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  age: z.number().min(13),\n})\n\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: { email: '', age: 0 },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: accountSchema,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nSchema paths are routed to matching fields. Parsed outputs are available by\nvalidator index in `schemaOutputs` during submit, for example\n`schemaOutputs[0]`. `value` remains the form's raw editable state rather than\nthe parsed output.\n\nFor custom schema routing, call a schema's safe parse API inside `run` and pass\nits issues to the provided `parseIssues` helper.\n\n## Validate related fields\n\nUse `watchFields` when one field's validity depends on another:\n\n```ts\nimport type { FieldValidators } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\ntype DateFormValues = { startDate: string; endDate: string }\n\nendDateValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n    watchFields: ['startDate'],\n    run: ({ value, formApi }) =>\n      value >= formApi.getFieldValue('startDate')\n        ? undefined\n        : 'End date must be on or after the start date',\n  },\n] satisfies FieldValidators<DateFormValues, 'endDate', string>\n```\n\n```html\n<ng-container\n  [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n  name=\"endDate\"\n  [validators]=\"endDateValidators\"\n  #field=\"field\"\n>\n  <input\n    type=\"date\"\n    [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n    [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n    (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n    [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n  />\n</ng-container>\n```\n\n## Validate a scoped form group\n\n`TanStackFormGroup` creates a v2 group for one concrete section of a form. The\ndirective exports its API as `formGroup`, and `fieldName` resolves a\ngroup-relative name to the concrete form path:\n\n```ts\nimport { TanStackField, TanStackFormGroup } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport type { FormGroupValidators } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nprofileValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: [],\n    run: ({ value }: { value: { name: string } }) =>\n      value.name.length >= 2 ? undefined : 'Enter a name',\n  },\n] satisfies FormGroupValidators<{ name: string }>\n\nsubmitGroup(event: SubmitEvent, group: { handleSubmit: () => unknown }) {\n  event.preventDefault()\n  void group.handleSubmit()\n}\n```\n\n```html\n<ng-container\n  [tanstackFormGroup]=\"form\"\n  name=\"profile\"\n  [validators]=\"profileValidators\"\n  #profile=\"formGroup\"\n>\n  <form (submit)=\"submitGroup($event, profile.api)\">\n    <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"profile.api\" name=\"name\" #name=\"field\">\n      <input\n        [name]=\"name.api.name\"\n        [value]=\"name.api.value\"\n        (input)=\"name.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n      />\n    </ng-container>\n\n    @for (error of profile.api.state.errors; track error) {\n    <span role=\"alert\">{{ error.message }}</span>\n    }\n    <button type=\"submit\">Continue</button>\n  </form>\n</ng-container>\n```\n\nImport both directives in the standalone component. Use a Form Group for a\nscoped section of one form; use reusable field mappings when a component must\nwork with different concrete field paths.\n\n## Return errors from submission\n\nEndpoint validation belongs in `onSubmit`. Return\n`createValidationError(...)` to feed server issues back into normal form state:\n\n```ts\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value, createValidationError }) => {\n    const result = await saveProfile(value)\n\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      return createValidationError({\n        form: 'Could not save the profile',\n        fields: { email: 'This email is already registered' },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return null\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Prevent invalid submission\n\n`form.handleSubmit()` skips `onSubmit` when validation fails and resolves with\nthe validation errors. `onSubmitInvalid` is currently available on form\ngroups; root-form support is planned but not yet implemented. Select\n`canSubmit` and `isSubmitting` as Angular signals to reflect that state in the\nsubmit UI:\n\n```ts\ncanSubmit = injectSelector(this.form, (state) => state.canSubmit)\nisSubmitting = injectSelector(this.form, (state) => state.isSubmitting)\n```\n\n```html\n<button type=\"submit\" [disabled]=\"!canSubmit() || isSubmitting()\">\n  {{ isSubmitting() ? 'Submitting…' : 'Submit' }}\n</button>\n```\n\nIf a disabled submit button would hide useful validation feedback, keep it\nfocusable with `aria-disabled` and let `handleSubmit()` report the issues.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: form-validation\ntitle: Form and Field Validation\n---\n\nTanStack Form supports synchronous, asynchronous, field-level, form-level, and\nStandard Schema validation. Every validator is an ordered object with a `run`\nimplementation and explicit `triggers`.\n\n## Choose when validation runs\n\nUse `change` for immediate feedback and `blur` for feedback after leaving an\ninput. Submission runs validators by default regardless of their configured\nchange and blur triggers.\n\n```ts\nageValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'] as const,\n    run: ({ value }: { value: number }) =>\n      value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n  },\n  {\n    triggers: ['blur'] as const,\n    run: ({ value }: { value: number }) =>\n      value >= 0 ? undefined : 'Age cannot be negative',\n  },\n]\n```\n\n```html\n<ng-container\n  [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n  name=\"age\"\n  [validators]=\"ageValidators\"\n  #field=\"field\"\n>\n  <label>\n    Age\n    <input\n      type=\"number\"\n      [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n      [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n      (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n      (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.valueAsNumber)\"\n      [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n    />\n    @for (error of field.api.errors; track error) {\n    <span role=\"alert\">{{ error.message }}</span>\n    }\n  </label>\n</ng-container>\n```\n\nAdditional controls include:\n\n- `runOnMount`: run once when the form is constructed or when a field or form\n  group first mounts.\n- `runOnSubmit`: disable or conditionally enable submit-time execution.\n- `triggerDebounceMs`: debounce change and blur execution.\n- `bailIfInvalid`: skip this and subsequent validators when an earlier one\n  failed.\n- trigger objects with `when`: enable a trigger conditionally.\n- `watchFields`: rerun a field validator when related fields trigger it.\n\n## Control when errors are visible\n\nValidation and presentation are separate. `errorVisibility` decides when\nfield issues appear in `field.api.errors`:\n\n```ts\nimport { injectForm } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  errorVisibility: ({ fieldState, state }) =>\n    fieldState.meta.isBlurred || state.submissionAttempts > 0,\n})\n```\n\nUse `field.api.meta.original.errors` for the unfiltered issues when debugging\nor building a custom visibility system.\n\n## Form-level validation\n\nA form validator can produce a form issue and route issues to typed field paths\nwith `createErrorMap`:\n\n```ts\nimport { injectForm, injectSelector } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    email: '',\n    phone: '',\n  },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n        const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n        if (!value.email && !value.phone) {\n          errors.form = 'Provide an email address or phone number'\n          errors.fields.email = 'Email is required when phone is empty'\n          errors.fields.phone = 'Phone is required when email is empty'\n        }\n\n        return errors\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nformErrors = injectSelector(this.form, (state) => state.errors)\n```\n\n`injectSelector` exposes form-level issues as an Angular signal. Lower-level\nintegrations can subscribe to `form.atom` directly. Field-routed issues appear\nin the corresponding `field.api.errors`.\n\n## Asynchronous validation and debouncing\n\n`run` may return a promise. Put cheap synchronous checks first and use\n`bailIfInvalid` to avoid unnecessary requests:\n\n```ts\nusernameValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'] as const,\n    run: ({ value }: { value: string }) =>\n      value.length >= 3 ? undefined : 'Use at least 3 characters',\n  },\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'] as const,\n    triggerDebounceMs: 500,\n    bailIfInvalid: true,\n    run: async ({ value }: { value: string }) => {\n      const available = await checkUsername(value)\n      return available ? undefined : 'That username is already taken'\n    },\n  },\n]\n```\n\nPass this array to the field with `[validators]=\"usernameValidators\"`.\nSubmit validation always runs immediately, even when a trigger is debounced.\n`field.api.meta.isValidating` and `form.state.isValidating` expose pending\nwork.\n\n## Standard Schema validation\n\nAny Standard Schema implementation can be supplied as `run`:\n\n```ts\nimport { injectForm } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst accountSchema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  age: z.number().min(13),\n})\n\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: { email: '', age: 0 },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: accountSchema,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nSchema paths are routed to matching fields. Parsed outputs are available by\nvalidator index in `schemaOutputs` during submit, for example\n`schemaOutputs[0]`. `value` remains the form's raw editable state rather than\nthe parsed output.\n\nFor custom schema routing, call a schema's safe parse API inside `run` and pass\nits issues to the provided `parseIssues` helper.\n\n## Validate related fields\n\nUse `watchFields` when one field's validity depends on another:\n\n```ts\nimport type { FieldValidators } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\ntype DateFormValues = { startDate: string; endDate: string }\n\nendDateValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n    watchFields: ['startDate'],\n    run: ({ value, formApi }) =>\n      value >= formApi.getFieldValue('startDate')\n        ? undefined\n        : 'End date must be on or after the start date',\n  },\n] satisfies FieldValidators<DateFormValues, 'endDate', string>\n```\n\n```html\n<ng-container\n  [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n  name=\"endDate\"\n  [validators]=\"endDateValidators\"\n  #field=\"field\"\n>\n  <input\n    type=\"date\"\n    [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n    [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n    (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n    [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n  />\n</ng-container>\n```\n\n## Validate a scoped form group\n\n`TanStackFormGroup` creates a v2 group for one concrete section of a form. The\ndirective exports its API as `formGroup`, and `fieldName` resolves a\ngroup-relative name to the concrete form path:\n\n```ts\nimport { TanStackField, TanStackFormGroup } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport type { FormGroupValidators } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nprofileValidators = [\n  {\n    triggers: [],\n    run: ({ value }: { value: { name: string } }) =>\n      value.name.length >= 2 ? undefined : 'Enter a name',\n  },\n] satisfies FormGroupValidators<{ name: string }>\n\nsubmitGroup(event: SubmitEvent, group: { handleSubmit: () => unknown }) {\n  event.preventDefault()\n  void group.handleSubmit()\n}\n```\n\n```html\n<ng-container\n  [tanstackFormGroup]=\"form\"\n  name=\"profile\"\n  [validators]=\"profileValidators\"\n  #profile=\"formGroup\"\n>\n  <form (submit)=\"submitGroup($event, profile.api)\">\n    <ng-container [tanstackField]=\"profile.api\" name=\"name\" #name=\"field\">\n      <input\n        [name]=\"name.api.name\"\n        [value]=\"name.api.value\"\n        (input)=\"name.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n      />\n    </ng-container>\n\n    @for (error of profile.api.state.errors; track error) {\n    <span role=\"alert\">{{ error.message }}</span>\n    }\n    <button type=\"submit\">Continue</button>\n  </form>\n</ng-container>\n```\n\nImport both directives in the standalone component. Use a Form Group for a\nscoped section of one form; use reusable field mappings when a component must\nwork with different concrete field paths.\n\n## Return errors from submission\n\nEndpoint validation belongs in `onSubmit`. Return\n`createValidationError(...)` to feed server issues back into normal form state:\n\n```ts\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value, createValidationError }) => {\n    const result = await saveProfile(value)\n\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      return createValidationError({\n        form: 'Could not save the profile',\n        fields: { email: 'This email is already registered' },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return null\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Prevent invalid submission\n\n`form.handleSubmit()` skips `onSubmit` when validation fails and resolves with\nthe validation errors. `onSubmitInvalid` is currently available on form\ngroups; root-form support is planned but not yet implemented. Select\n`canSubmit` and `isSubmitting` as Angular signals to reflect that state in the\nsubmit UI:\n\n```ts\ncanSubmit = injectSelector(this.form, (state) => state.canSubmit)\nisSubmitting = injectSelector(this.form, (state) => state.isSubmitting)\n```\n\n```html\n<button type=\"submit\" [disabled]=\"!canSubmit() || isSubmitting()\">\n  {{ isSubmitting() ? 'Submitting…' : 'Submit' }}\n</button>\n```\n\nIf a disabled submit button would hide useful validation feedback, keep it\nfocusable with `aria-disabled` and let `handleSubmit()` report the issues.\n"}
